# Meta description (required)

Every shippable HTML page must include in `<head>`:

```html
<meta name="description" content="Descriptive, keyword-rich text that talks about the page content goes here.">
```

Rules:

- Write real page-specific copy (product name + what this page does + plain keywords).
- Prefer ~120–160 characters; never leave the placeholder text.
- Public marketing pages: indexable copy. Signed-in /admin/console pages: still include a description (often with `noindex`).
- If the app uses a shared layout/`seo()` helper, put the descriptions there — do not skip pages that go through that layout.
- When adding a new view or route, add its description in the same change.

Family Shield Pro: keep the “guidance, not a guarantee / never a safe stamp” voice in public descriptions.
